=begin

  perfume.lic -- keep a perfume / cologne vial active on yourself at all times.

  How it works
    * Timer based, and the timer survives logout. A GemStone perfume lasts
      4 hours; this script re-applies every 3h45m (UserVars.perfume_reapply_hours)
      so it always refreshes before the scent can lapse.
    * The time of the last application is saved in UserVars (per character, in
      Lich's database), so when you log back in it knows how long has really
      elapsed -- a scent keeps ticking while you're logged out. On login it
      re-applies immediately if the interval already passed, otherwise it waits
      out the remaining time.
    * Backup: a DownstreamHook also watches for the standard wear-off line and
      re-applies the instant it appears (confirmed verbatim in the logs):
          "The subtle scent which had been clinging to you dissipates."
    * Refresh sequence:
        pause every OTHER running script except a keep-running list
        wait until at least one hand is free
        GET MY <vial> FROM MY <bag>
        POUR MY <vial> ON <self>
        PUT MY <vial> IN MY <bag>
        resume exactly the scripts we paused (always, even if interrupted)

  Pausing
    Rather than maintain an ever-growing list of hunting scripts, this pauses
    ALL running scripts during the brief refresh EXCEPT those on a keep-running
    list (heals, networking, HUD/display, logging, infra, and perfume itself).
    That way any hunting / combat / loot script you run is covered automatically.
    Only scripts that were actually running AND not already paused are touched,
    and they're resumed when the refresh ends -- so nothing is left paused.

  Usage
    ;perfume                 -- start the monitor (apply if due, then keep timing)
    ;perfume now             -- apply immediately (resets the timer), keep monitoring
    ;perfume once            -- apply once and exit (no monitor)
    ;perfume check           -- run one SNIFF and report active / inactive
    ;perfume status          -- show settings + time until next re-apply
    ;perfume stop            -- stop the monitor
    ;perfume measure         -- report applications remaining (MEASURE)
    ;perfume scan            -- shifting vial: cycle RUB and record every scent (quiet)
    ;perfume reset           -- wipe the recorded scent catalog and start over
    ;perfume scents          -- review the recorded scent list (numbered summaries)
    ;perfume scent <n>       -- full first/third-person detail for scent number <n>
    ;perfume goto <n>        -- switch the vial to catalog scent number <n>
    ;perfume help            -- show usage
    ;perfume set mode <bag|worn> -- bagged vial (needs a free hand) vs worn item
    ;perfume set vial <name> -- set the vial / worn-item name
    ;perfume set bag <name>  -- set the bag name (bag mode only)
    ;perfume set verb <verb> -- apply verb (default pour); e.g. apply, dab, spray
    ;perfume set warn <n>    -- warn when applications drop to <n> or fewer
    ;perfume set hours <n>   -- set the re-apply interval in hours
    ;perfume set keep <csv>  -- set the keep-running list

  Modes
    bag  (default) -- the perfume is a vial kept in a container. To apply, the
                      script needs a free hand: it GETs the vial, POURs it on
                      you, and PUTs it back. Requires vial + bag names.
    worn           -- the perfume is a worn item (locket / bottle / etc.) that
                      stays equipped. To apply, the script just POURs it on you
                      in place: no free hand, no GET/PUT. Requires only the
                      item name (set it with ';perfume set vial <name>').

  The vial/item name must be what the game recognizes: "pour my <name>" (and in
  bag mode "get my <name>") has to work by hand. "hollow vial" will NOT match
  "a pristine hollow bone vial..." -- use "hollow bone vial" (or whatever works).

  On first use it has nothing configured and will ask you to set up; it won't
  try to apply anything until you do.

  Configuration (UserVars -- set via ';perfume set ...', persists per character)
    UserVars.perfume_mode           "bag" (default) or "worn"
    UserVars.perfume_vial           (required) vial/item name -- ;perfume set vial
    UserVars.perfume_bag            (required in bag mode)     -- ;perfume set bag
    UserVars.perfume_verb           default: "pour" -- the verb used to apply
    UserVars.perfume_warn_at        default: 50 -- warn when applications <= this
    UserVars.perfume_reapply_hours  default: 3.75   (3h45m; scent lasts 4h)
    UserVars.perfume_keep_scripts   CSV of scripts to LEAVE RUNNING during the
        refresh. Everything else that's running gets paused briefly. Edit this
        to add anything you never want paused. perfume itself is always kept.
    UserVars.perfume_bottomless     (internal) cached true/false from MEASURE.
    UserVars.perfume_apps_left      (internal) last known applications remaining.
    UserVars.perfume_last_applied   (internal) epoch time of last application.

  Limited-application perfumes
    Some perfumes have a finite number of applications (MEASURE shows e.g.
    "1994 of a maximum 2000 applications"); others are bottomless. After each
    apply (bag mode) the script MEASUREs the item and warns when the count
    falls to UserVars.perfume_warn_at or below. The warning is a bordered box
    highlighted in monsterbold so it's hard to miss. Once it sees "bottomless"
    it stops measuring. Use ';perfume measure' to check on demand.

  Shifting vials (many scents in one item, ~300)
    A "shifting vial" cycles through many scents (RUB = next scent). The game
    gives no per-scent number -- the only numbers are the 5 favorite slots
    (WHISPER/NUDGE/PONDER) -- so this script assigns its own catalog numbers in
    discovery order. RUB itself does NOT print the scent, so each step the scan
    SNIFFs the current scent (short summary) and ANALYZEs it (full first/third-
    person text), then RUBs to the next. It runs QUIETLY
    (Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml), so the ~300 SNIFF/ANALYZE/RUB rounds don't
    spam the screen -- only a periodic progress count shows. Results save --
    numbered in discovery order -- to a per-character file:
        DATA_DIR/perfume_scents_<character>.json
    Because RUB returns to the starting scent, scanning leaves the vial where
    it began. To avoid the game's flood disconnect, scanning paces itself
    (UserVars.perfume_scan_delay, default 5s between scents) and saves the
    catalog incrementally every 10 scents, so a dropped connection mid-scan
    keeps what it already found. A full ~300-scent scan takes a while -- run it
    when you're parked somewhere safe. While scanning, a small GTK progress
    window shows the live count (falls back to text updates if GTK is
    unavailable).
      ;perfume scents     -- numbered list of short summaries
      ;perfume scent <n>  -- full first/third-person detail for one number
      ;perfume goto <n>   -- switch the vial to that catalog scent
      ;perfume reset      -- wipe the saved catalog so the next scan is clean
    A new ';perfume scan' always starts over from scratch (it cycles the whole
    wheel from wherever the vial currently is), so cancelled scans don't
    corrupt a later one -- but ';perfume reset' clears any leftover partial data
    if you want a guaranteed clean slate first.
    Because the catalog is stored in RUB-cycle order, 'goto' finds the current
    scent (SNIFF), computes how many RUBs reach the target, and RUBs exactly
    that many times (with a search fallback if the catalog is out of date).
    RUBs are paced by UserVars.perfume_goto_delay (default 1.5s) to avoid a
    flood disconnect, so a far jump can take a couple minutes. The vial only
    cycles forward, so for scents you use a lot, store them as favorites
    (NUDGE) and WHISPER the number for an instant switch.

  Author : Mystienne
  Version: 0.7.0

=end

DEFAULT_KEEP = %w[
  lnet ecure ecleanse ecaster absorb creaturebar back-in-black injurywatch
  room-buddy gemtracker lumnismon lumnisdonate uberbar_eo spellactive
  song-manager reactive alias version dependency repository lich5-update
  elogin charsetup go2 go2locate
].join(',')

# NOTE: vial and bag are intentionally NOT defaulted -- the script asks you to
# configure them (the names must match your specific item / container).
UserVars.perfume_reapply_hours ||= 3.75
UserVars.perfume_keep_scripts  ||= DEFAULT_KEEP
UserVars.perfume_mode          ||= 'bag'
UserVars.perfume_verb          ||= 'pour'
UserVars.perfume_warn_at       ||= 50
UserVars.perfume_scan_delay    ||= 5
UserVars.perfume_goto_delay    ||= 1.5

VIAL          = UserVars.perfume_vial.to_s.strip
BAG           = UserVars.perfume_bag.to_s.strip
MODE          = UserVars.perfume_mode.to_s.strip.downcase
MODE          = 'bag' unless %w[bag worn].include?(MODE)
VERB          = (UserVars.perfume_verb.to_s.strip.downcase.empty? ? 'pour' : UserVars.perfume_verb.to_s.strip.downcase)
WARN_AT       = UserVars.perfume_warn_at.to_i
SCAN_DELAY    = [UserVars.perfume_scan_delay.to_f, 1.0].max # seconds between scents during a scan
GOTO_DELAY    = [UserVars.perfume_goto_delay.to_f, 0.5].max # seconds between RUBs while switching scents
REAPPLY_HOURS = UserVars.perfume_reapply_hours.to_f
REAPPLY_HOURS = 3.75 if REAPPLY_HOURS <= 0
REAPPLY_SECS  = (REAPPLY_HOURS * 3600).to_i
# Names we never pause: the keep list, plus this script itself.
KEEP_SCRIPTS  = (UserVars.perfume_keep_scripts.to_s.split(',').map { |n| n.strip.downcase } + ['perfume']).reject(&:empty?).uniq

require 'json'

# Catalog of scents for a "shifting vial" (the kind that cycles many scents via
# RUB). Saved per character in its own file, since a given vial's list is fixed.
SCENT_FILE = File.join(DATA_DIR, "perfume_scents_#{checkname.to_s.downcase}.json")

# Generic "you are wearing no scent" response -- same for every perfume.
NO_SCENT_RE = /think\*? you smell okay|smell okay, but then|doesn't everybody/i
# Apply confirmation -- broad so it works across verbs (pour/apply/dab/spray/...).
APPLY_OK_RE   = /You pour a few drops|You (?:apply|dab|spray|splash|smear|rub|anoint|spritz|brush|wipe|put)\b|veil of scent|enshroud|now (?:carries|bears|wear)|a (?:faint|subtle|light|delicate) (?:scent|fragrance|aroma)/i
APPLY_FAIL_RE = /what\?|^What were you|^I could not find|^You don't have|^You can't|^There (?:is|are) no/i

sub = script.vars[1].to_s.downcase

def print_help
  respond ''
  respond '=== perfume: usage ==='
  respond '  ;perfume                  start monitoring (apply if due, keep timing)'
  respond '  ;perfume now              apply immediately, then keep monitoring'
  respond '  ;perfume once             apply once and exit'
  respond '  ;perfume check            sniff once and report active / inactive'
  respond '  ;perfume measure          show applications remaining (MEASURE)'
  respond '  ;perfume scan             shifting vial: RUB through and record all scents (quiet)'
  respond '  ;perfume reset            wipe the recorded scent catalog (start over)'
  respond '  ;perfume scents           review the recorded scent list (numbered summaries)'
  respond '  ;perfume scent <n>        full first/third-person detail for scent number <n>'
  respond '  ;perfume goto <n>         switch the vial to catalog scent number <n>'
  respond '  ;perfume status           show settings + time until next re-apply'
  respond '  ;perfume stop             stop the monitor'
  respond '  ;perfume help             this help'
  respond '  --- settings (saved per character) ---'
  respond '  ;perfume set mode <bag|worn>  bag = get/pour/put a vial (needs a free hand)'
  respond '                                worn = just apply a worn item (no free hand)'
  respond '  ;perfume set vial <name>  e.g. ;perfume set vial hollow bone vial'
  respond '  ;perfume set bag <name>   e.g. ;perfume set bag spidersilk bag  (bag mode only)'
  respond '  ;perfume set verb <verb>  apply verb (default pour); e.g. apply, dab, spray'
  respond '  ;perfume set warn <n>     warn when applications drop to <n> or fewer (default 50)'
  respond '  ;perfume set scandelay <s>  seconds between scents while scanning (default 5)'
  respond '  ;perfume set gotodelay <s>  seconds between RUBs while switching (default 1.5)'
  respond '  ;perfume set hours <n>    e.g. ;perfume set hours 3.75'
  respond '  ;perfume set keep <csv>   scripts to leave running during a refresh'
  respond "  tip: the vial/item name must match how the game sees it -- '<verb> my <name>'"
  respond "       (and in bag mode 'get my <name>') has to work by hand."
  respond ''
end

def prompt_setup
  respond ''
  if MODE == 'worn'
    respond ';perfume: not configured yet -- set the worn item to apply.'
    respond '  The name must work with POUR by hand, e.g.:'
    respond '    ;perfume set vial perfume bottle'
  else
    respond ';perfume: not configured yet -- please set your vial and bag first.'
    respond '  The names must work with GET by hand, e.g.:'
    respond '    ;perfume set vial hollow bone vial'
    respond '    ;perfume set bag spidersilk bag'
  end
  respond '  Then start it with:  ;perfume'
  respond '  (;perfume set mode worn  if your perfume is a worn item, not a bagged vial.)'
  respond '  (;perfume help shows all options.)'
  respond ''
end

# Help / unknown sub-command -> show usage instead of starting the monitor.
VALID_SUBS = %w[start now once check measure scan reset scents scent goto switch list status stop set help].freeze
if sub == 'help' || (!sub.empty? && !VALID_SUBS.include?(sub))
  print_help
  exit
end

if sub == 'set'
  parts = script.vars[0].to_s.split(/\s+/)
  key   = parts[1].to_s.downcase
  value = parts[2..-1].to_a.join(' ').strip
  if key.empty? || value.empty?
    respond ''
    respond ';perfume: usage -- ;perfume set <mode|vial|bag|verb|warn|scandelay|gotodelay|hours|keep> <value>'
    respond ''
    exit
  end
  respond ''
  case key
  when 'mode'
    v = value.downcase
    if %w[bag worn].include?(v)
      UserVars.perfume_mode = v
      respond ";perfume: mode set to '#{v}'#{v == 'worn' ? ' (worn item -- no free hand, no get/put)' : ' (bagged vial -- get/pour/put)'}."
    else
      respond ";perfume: mode must be 'bag' or 'worn'."
      respond ''
      exit
    end
  when 'vial', 'item'
    UserVars.perfume_vial = value
    UserVars.perfume_bottomless = nil # different item -- forget cached MEASURE data
    UserVars.perfume_apps_left  = nil
    respond ";perfume: #{MODE == 'worn' ? 'item' : 'vial'} set to '#{value}'."
  when 'bag'
    UserVars.perfume_bag = value
    respond ";perfume: bag set to '#{value}'."
  when 'verb'
    UserVars.perfume_verb = value.downcase.split.first
    respond ";perfume: apply verb set to '#{UserVars.perfume_verb}'."
  when 'warn'
    UserVars.perfume_warn_at = value.to_i
    respond ";perfume: low-application warning set at #{value.to_i} or fewer."
  when 'scandelay'
    UserVars.perfume_scan_delay = value.to_f
    respond ";perfume: scan delay set to #{value.to_f}s between scents (lower = faster but risks a flood disconnect)."
  when 'gotodelay'
    UserVars.perfume_goto_delay = value.to_f
    respond ";perfume: goto delay set to #{value.to_f}s between RUBs."
  when 'hours'
    UserVars.perfume_reapply_hours = value.to_f
    respond ";perfume: re-apply interval set to #{value.to_f}h."
  when 'keep'
    UserVars.perfume_keep_scripts = value
    respond ";perfume: keep-running list set to: #{value}"
  else
    respond ";perfume: unknown setting '#{key}'. Use mode, vial, bag, verb, warn, scandelay, gotodelay, hours, or keep."
    respond ''
    exit
  end
  if Script.list.any? { |s| s.name == 'perfume' && s != Script.current }
    respond ';perfume: restart the monitor (;k perfume then ;perfume) for the change to take effect.'
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

if sub == 'stop'
  other = Script.list.find { |s| s.name == 'perfume' && s != Script.current }
  if other
    kill_script('perfume')
    respond ';perfume: stopped.'
  else
    respond ';perfume: not running.'
  end
  exit
end

if sub == 'status'
  last = UserVars.perfume_last_applied.to_i
  respond ''
  respond '=== perfume ==='
  respond "  mode          : #{MODE}#{MODE == 'worn' ? ' (worn item -- no free hand)' : ' (bagged vial)'}"
  respond "  #{MODE == 'worn' ? 'item' : 'vial'}          : #{VIAL.empty? ? '(not set -- ;perfume set vial <name>)' : VIAL}"
  respond "  bag           : #{BAG.empty? ? '(not set -- ;perfume set bag <name>)' : BAG}" if MODE == 'bag'
  respond "  apply verb    : #{VERB}"
  respond "  reapply every : #{REAPPLY_HOURS}h (#{REAPPLY_SECS}s)"
  if UserVars.perfume_bottomless == true
    respond '  applications  : bottomless (infinite)'
  elsif !UserVars.perfume_apps_left.nil?
    respond "  applications  : #{UserVars.perfume_apps_left.to_i} left (warn at #{WARN_AT})"
  else
    respond "  applications  : unknown (run ;perfume measure)"
  end
  respond "  keep running  : #{KEEP_SCRIPTS.join(', ')}"
  if last > 0
    ago = Time.now.to_i - last
    due = REAPPLY_SECS - ago
    respond "  last applied  : #{ago / 60} min ago"
    respond "  next re-apply : #{due > 0 ? "in #{due / 60} min" : 'overdue (now)'}"
  else
    respond '  last applied  : never recorded'
  end
  running_other = Script.list.any? { |s| s.name == 'perfume' && s != Script.current }
  respond "  running       : #{running_other ? 'yes' : 'no'}"
  respond ''
  exit
end

$perfume_paused = []

def has_free_hand?
  GameObj.right_hand.id.nil? || GameObj.left_hand.id.nil?
end

def wait_for_free_hand
  return if has_free_hand?
  echo 'perfume: both hands full -- waiting for a free hand before refreshing scent.'
  attempts = 0
  until has_free_hand?
    sleep 2
    attempts += 1
    break if attempts > 150 # ~5 min safety cap
  end
end

# Returns true (active), false (inactive), or nil (couldn't tell).
def perfume_active?
  line = dothistimeout "sniff #{checkname}", 5, /^You /
  return nil if line.nil?
  !(line =~ NO_SCENT_RE)
end

# Pause everything currently running except the keep list / perfume itself.
# Returns the names we actually paused so we can resume exactly those.
def pause_other_scripts(keep)
  paused = []
  Script.list.each do |s|
    next if s == Script.current
    next if keep.include?(s.name.to_s.downcase)
    next if s.paused?
    pause_script(s.name)
    paused << s.name
  end
  paused
end

def resume_scripts(paused)
  return if paused.nil?
  paused.each { |name| unpause_script(name) if Script.running?(name) }
end

# Apply the perfume onto yourself using the configured verb. True on success.
def apply_on_self
  cmd = "#{VERB} my #{VIAL} on #{checkname}"
  r = dothistimeout cmd, 5, /#{APPLY_OK_RE.source}|#{APPLY_FAIL_RE.source}/i
  if r.nil?
    echo "perfume: '#{cmd}' got no recognizable response. If your perfume uses a verb"
    echo "perfume: other than '#{VERB}', set it with ';perfume set verb <verb>'."
    return false
  end
  if r =~ APPLY_FAIL_RE
    echo "perfume: apply failed (game said: #{r.strip})."
    return false
  end
  true
end

# MEASURE the perfume. Returns :bottomless, [remaining, max], or nil (unknown).
def measure_perfume
  line = dothistimeout "measure my #{VIAL}", 5,
                       /bottomless|infinite amount|currently has \d+ of a maximum \d+|^Measure what|^What were you|^I could not find/i
  return nil if line.nil?
  return :bottomless if line =~ /bottomless|infinite amount/i
  return [$1.to_i, $2.to_i] if line =~ /currently has (\d+) of a maximum (\d+)/i
  nil
end

# --- shifting-vial scent catalog -------------------------------------------
#
# All scan commands run quietly via Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml so the ~300
# RUB/ANALYZE pairs don't spam the screen. For each scent we keep a short
# summary (for the numbered list) and the full first/third-person text (from
# ANALYZE) for the per-number detail view.

# Current scent's short summary, via SNIFF. Returns text or nil.
def scent_summary_sniff
  lines = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("sniff my #{VIAL}", /detect the faint scent of|You sniff|Sniff what|rephrase|don't have|can't/, /<prompt/)
  line  = lines.find { |l| l =~ /detect the faint scent of/i }
  return $1.strip if line && line =~ /detect the faint scent of (.+?)\.?\s*$/i
  nil
end

# Diagnostic: the plain-text response to 'sniff my <vial>' (for failure messages).
def sniff_debug
  lines = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("sniff my #{VIAL}", /sniff|scent|rephrase|can't|don't have|don't see|What were/i, /<prompt/)
  lines.map { |l| l.gsub(/<[^>]*>/, '').strip }.reject(&:empty?).join(' ')[0, 200]
rescue StandardError => e
  "error: #{e.message}"
end

# Advance to the next scent. RUB does NOT announce the scent (just "shimmer
# briefly"), so we read the new scent separately with SNIFF afterward.
def advance_scent
  Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("rub my #{VIAL}", /shimmer briefly|Rub what|I could not find|You can't/, /<prompt/)
end

# ANALYZE the current scent; return [first_person, third_person] (may be nil).
def scent_analyze
  lines = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("analyze my #{VIAL}", /You analyze the/, /<prompt/)
  first = third = nil
  lines.each do |ln|
    first = $1.strip if ln =~ /First-person:\s*(.+?)\s*$/
    third = $1.strip if ln =~ /Third-person:\s*(.+?)\s*$/
  end
  [first, third]
end

# --- optional GTK progress window for the scan -----------------------------
$perfume_scan_win = nil
$perfume_scan_lbl = nil
$perfume_scan_bar = nil
$perfume_scan_gui = false

def scan_window_open
  require 'gtk3'
  Gtk.queue do
    $perfume_scan_win = Gtk::Window.new(:toplevel)
    $perfume_scan_win.set_keep_above(true)
    $perfume_scan_win.set_title('Perfume Scan')
    $perfume_scan_win.set_default_size(420, 110)
    box = Gtk::Box.new(:vertical, 4)
    [:set_margin_top, :set_margin_bottom, :set_margin_start, :set_margin_end].each { |m| box.send(m, 8) }
    $perfume_scan_lbl = Gtk::Label.new('Starting scan...')
    $perfume_scan_lbl.set_xalign(0.0)
    $perfume_scan_lbl.set_line_wrap(true)
    $perfume_scan_lbl.set_max_width_chars(60)
    $perfume_scan_bar = Gtk::ProgressBar.new
    $perfume_scan_bar.set_show_text(true)
    $perfume_scan_bar.set_text('0 scents')
    box.pack_start($perfume_scan_lbl, expand: false, fill: false, padding: 0)
    box.pack_start($perfume_scan_bar, expand: false, fill: false, padding: 0)
    $perfume_scan_win.signal_connect('destroy') { $perfume_scan_win = nil }
    $perfume_scan_win.add(box)
    $perfume_scan_win.show_all
  end
  $perfume_scan_gui = true
rescue StandardError, LoadError => e
  echo "perfume: progress window unavailable (#{e.message}); scanning with text updates only."
  $perfume_scan_gui = false
end

def scan_window_update(n, summary = nil)
  return unless $perfume_scan_gui
  Gtk.queue do
    begin
      $perfume_scan_lbl.set_text("Recorded #{n} scents#{summary ? "\nlatest: #{summary}" : ''}") if $perfume_scan_lbl
      if $perfume_scan_bar
        $perfume_scan_bar.pulse
        $perfume_scan_bar.set_text("#{n} scents")
      end
    rescue StandardError
      nil # window may have been closed mid-update
    end
  end
end

def scan_window_close(final = nil)
  return unless $perfume_scan_gui
  Gtk.queue do
    begin
      if $perfume_scan_win
        if final && $perfume_scan_lbl
          $perfume_scan_lbl.set_text(final)
          $perfume_scan_bar.set_fraction(1.0) if $perfume_scan_bar
        else
          $perfume_scan_win.destroy
        end
      end
    rescue StandardError
      nil
    end
  end
end

# Cycle the whole wheel once: SNIFF the current scent (summary) + ANALYZE it
# (full first/third), then RUB to the next. Stops when a summary repeats (we've
# come full circle) and caps for safety. Since RUB wraps back to the starting
# scent, the vial is left where it began.
def scan_scents
  scents = []
  seen   = {}
  500.times do
    summary = scent_summary_sniff
    break if summary.nil?            # can't read -- bail rather than spin
    break if seen[summary.downcase]  # looped back to a scent we've recorded
    seen[summary.downcase] = true
    sleep 1
    f, t = scent_analyze
    scents << { 'n' => scents.size + 1, 'summary' => summary, 'first' => f, 'third' => t }
    # Save incrementally so a disconnect mid-scan doesn't lose progress.
    save_scents(scents) if (scents.size % 10).zero?
    respond ";perfume: scanning... recorded #{scents.size}" if (scents.size % 25).zero?
    scan_window_update(scents.size, summary)
    sleep 1
    advance_scent
    sleep SCAN_DELAY # pace commands to avoid the game's flood disconnect
  end
  scents
end

def save_scents(list)
  File.open(SCENT_FILE, 'w') do |f|
    f.write(JSON.pretty_generate('vial' => VIAL, 'scanned_at' => Time.now.to_s, 'scents' => list))
  end
end

def load_scents
  return nil unless File.exist?(SCENT_FILE)
  JSON.parse(File.read(SCENT_FILE))
rescue StandardError
  nil
end

# Switch the vial to catalog scent #n. The catalog is in RUB-cycle order, so we
# find the current scent's index (via SNIFF), compute the forward distance to
# the target, and RUB exactly that many times. If the current scent isn't in
# the catalog (stale data) or the result doesn't match, fall back to RUBbing
# around the wheel until the target summary appears. Returns true on success.
def goto_scent(scents, n)
  total  = scents.size
  target = scents[n - 1]['summary'].to_s
  cur    = scent_summary_sniff
  if cur && (idx = scents.index { |h| h['summary'].to_s.downcase == cur.downcase })
    dist = ((n - 1) - idx) % total
    respond ";perfume: #{dist} rub#{dist == 1 ? '' : 's'} away (~#{(dist * GOTO_DELAY).round}s)..." if dist > 5
    dist.times { advance_scent; sleep GOTO_DELAY }
    now = scent_summary_sniff
    return true if now && now.downcase == target.downcase
  end
  # Fallback search around the whole wheel (handles a stale/out-of-order catalog).
  (total + 2).times do
    c = scent_summary_sniff
    return true if c && c.downcase == target.downcase
    advance_scent
    sleep GOTO_DELAY
  end
  false
end

# Loud, bordered, monsterbold-highlighted low-applications warning.
def perfume_low_warning(rem, max)
  lines = [
    'PERFUME RUNNING LOW',
    "#{rem} of #{max} applications remaining",
    "restock: #{VIAL}"
  ]
  inner  = lines.map(&:length).max + 6 # 3 spaces padding each side
  border = '*' * (inner + 2)
  begin
    mb_s = monsterbold_start
    mb_e = monsterbold_end
  rescue StandardError
    mb_s = ''
    mb_e = ''
  end
  _respond ''
  _respond "#{mb_s}#{border}#{mb_e}"
  lines.each { |ln| _respond "#{mb_s}*#{ln.center(inner)}*#{mb_e}" }
  _respond "#{mb_s}#{border}#{mb_e}"
  _respond ''
end

# Best-effort application count + low warning. Skips MEASURE once we know the
# item is bottomless (no point repeating it every cycle).
def check_applications
  return if UserVars.perfume_bottomless == true
  result = measure_perfume
  case result
  when :bottomless
    UserVars.perfume_bottomless = true
    UserVars.perfume_apps_left  = nil
  when Array
    UserVars.perfume_bottomless = false
    rem, max = result
    UserVars.perfume_apps_left  = rem
    perfume_low_warning(rem, max) if rem <= WARN_AT
  end
end

# Bagged vial: needs a free hand; get it out, apply, (measure), put it back.
def apply_from_bag
  wait_for_free_hand
  r = dothistimeout "get my #{VIAL} from my #{BAG}", 5,
                    /^You remove|^Get what\?|^What were you|^I could not find|^You don't have|^There is nothing/i
  unless r =~ /^You remove/i
    echo "perfume: could not GET vial (game said: #{r ? r.strip : 'no response'})."
    echo "perfume: set the right names with ';perfume set vial <name>' and ';perfume set bag <name>'."
    echo "perfume: current vial='#{VIAL}', bag='#{BAG}'.  Try a name that works with 'get my <name>' by hand."
    return false
  end
  applied = apply_on_self
  check_applications # while it's still in hand
  dothistimeout "put my #{VIAL} in my #{BAG}", 5,
                /^You put|^Put what|^I could not find/i
  applied
end

# Worn item: no free hand, no get/put -- just apply it in place.
def apply_worn
  applied = apply_on_self
  check_applications # best effort (some worn items can't be measured)
  applied
end

# Applies the perfume. On success it stamps UserVars.perfume_last_applied
# (which both the timer and the wear-off hook rely on) and returns true.
def refresh_perfume
  $perfume_paused = pause_other_scripts(KEEP_SCRIPTS)
  begin
    applied = (MODE == 'worn') ? apply_worn : apply_from_bag
    UserVars.perfume_last_applied = Time.now.to_i if applied
    applied ? true : false
  ensure
    resume_scripts($perfume_paused)
    $perfume_paused = []
  end
end

if sub == 'check'
  respond ''
  case perfume_active?
  when true  then respond ';perfume: ACTIVE -- a scent is currently on you.'
  when false then respond ';perfume: NOT active -- no scent detected.'
  else            respond ';perfume: could not tell (no SNIFF response in time).'
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

if sub == 'measure'
  if VIAL.empty?
    prompt_setup
    exit
  end
  respond ''
  paused  = pause_other_scripts(KEEP_SCRIPTS)
  got_out = false
  begin
    if MODE == 'bag' && !BAG.empty?
      wait_for_free_hand
      r = dothistimeout "get my #{VIAL} from my #{BAG}", 5,
                        /^You remove|^Get what\?|^What were you|^I could not find|^You don't have|^There is nothing/i
      got_out = !!(r =~ /^You remove/i)
      echo "perfume: could not GET vial (game said: #{r ? r.strip : 'no response'})." unless got_out
    end
    result = measure_perfume
    case result
    when :bottomless
      UserVars.perfume_bottomless = true
      UserVars.perfume_apps_left  = nil
      respond ";perfume: #{VIAL} is bottomless (infinite applications)."
    when Array
      UserVars.perfume_bottomless = false
      UserVars.perfume_apps_left  = result[0]
      respond ";perfume: #{result[0]} of #{result[1]} applications left in #{VIAL}."
      perfume_low_warning(result[0], result[1]) if result[0] <= WARN_AT
    else
      respond ";perfume: couldn't read an application count from MEASURE."
    end
  ensure
    dothistimeout("put my #{VIAL} in my #{BAG}", 5, /^You put|^Put what|^I could not find/i) if got_out
    resume_scripts(paused)
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Wipe the saved scent catalog so the next scan starts completely fresh.
if sub == 'reset'
  respond ''
  if File.exist?(SCENT_FILE)
    begin
      File.delete(SCENT_FILE)
      respond ";perfume: cleared the recorded scent catalog."
      respond "  (#{SCENT_FILE})"
      respond "  run ';perfume scan' to build a fresh one."
    rescue StandardError => e
      respond ";perfume: could not delete the catalog file -- #{e.message}"
    end
  else
    respond ';perfume: no recorded scent catalog to clear -- nothing to reset.'
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Review the saved scent catalog -- numbered summaries (no game commands).
if sub == 'scents' || sub == 'list'
  data = load_scents
  respond ''
  if data.nil? || data['scents'].to_a.empty?
    respond ";perfume: no scents recorded yet -- run ';perfume scan' while wearing/holding the vial."
  else
    respond "=== recorded scents for #{data['vial']} (#{data['scents'].size}) ==="
    data['scents'].each { |h| respond format('  %3d. %s', h['n'].to_i, h['summary']) }
    respond "  full detail for one: ;perfume scent <number>"
    respond "  (scanned #{data['scanned_at']})"
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Full first/third-person detail for a single recorded scent number.
if sub == 'scent'
  n    = script.vars[2].to_i
  data = load_scents
  respond ''
  if data.nil? || data['scents'].to_a.empty?
    respond ";perfume: no scents recorded yet -- run ';perfume scan' first."
  elsif n < 1 || n > data['scents'].size
    respond ";perfume: pick a number from 1 to #{data['scents'].size} (see ;perfume scents)."
  else
    h = data['scents'][n - 1]
    respond "=== #{data['vial']} -- scent ##{h['n']} of #{data['scents'].size} ==="
    respond "  summary     : #{h['summary']}"
    respond "  first-person: #{h['first'] || '(not recorded)'}"
    respond "  third-person: #{h['third'] || '(not recorded)'}"
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Switch the vial to a recorded catalog scent by our number.
if sub == 'goto' || sub == 'switch'
  n    = script.vars[2].to_i
  data = load_scents
  respond ''
  if data.nil? || data['scents'].to_a.empty?
    respond ";perfume: no scents recorded yet -- run ';perfume scan' first."
    respond ''
    exit
  end
  if n < 1 || n > data['scents'].size
    respond ";perfume: pick a number from 1 to #{data['scents'].size} (see ;perfume scents)."
    respond ''
    exit
  end
  if VIAL.empty?
    prompt_setup
    exit
  end
  respond ";perfume: switching to scent ##{n} (#{data['scents'][n - 1]['summary']})..."
  paused  = pause_other_scripts(KEEP_SCRIPTS)
  got_out = false
  ok      = false
  begin
    if MODE == 'bag' && !BAG.empty?
      wait_for_free_hand
      r = dothistimeout "get my #{VIAL} from my #{BAG}", 5,
                        /^You remove|^Get what\?|^What were you|^I could not find|^You don't have|^There is nothing/i
      got_out = !!(r =~ /^You remove/i)
      echo "perfume: could not GET vial (game said: #{r ? r.strip : 'no response'})." unless got_out
    end
    ok = goto_scent(data['scents'], n)
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "perfume: goto error -- #{e.message}"
  ensure
    dothistimeout("put my #{VIAL} in my #{BAG}", 5, /^You put|^Put what|^I could not find/i) if got_out
    resume_scripts(paused)
  end
  if ok
    respond ";perfume: now wearing scent ##{n}: #{data['scents'][n - 1]['summary']}"
  else
    respond ";perfume: couldn't reach scent ##{n} -- the catalog may be out of date; try ';perfume scan' again."
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Scan a shifting vial: RUB through every scent once and record them.
if sub == 'scan'
  if VIAL.empty?
    prompt_setup
    exit
  end
  respond ''
  respond ";perfume: scanning all scents on your #{VIAL} -- this RUBs through the whole"
  respond '  wheel once, so do it somewhere quiet. Other scripts are paused meanwhile.'
  scan_window_open
  paused  = pause_other_scripts(KEEP_SCRIPTS)
  got_out = false
  scents  = []
  begin
    if MODE == 'bag' && !BAG.empty?
      wait_for_free_hand
      r = dothistimeout "get my #{VIAL} from my #{BAG}", 5,
                        /^You remove|^Get what\?|^What were you|^I could not find|^You don't have|^There is nothing/i
      got_out = !!(r =~ /^You remove/i)
      echo "perfume: could not GET vial (game said: #{r ? r.strip : 'no response'})." unless got_out
    end
    scents = scan_scents
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "perfume: scan error -- #{e.message}"
  ensure
    dothistimeout("put my #{VIAL} in my #{BAG}", 5, /^You put|^Put what|^I could not find/i) if got_out
    resume_scripts(paused)
  end
  if scents.empty?
    scan_window_close
    respond ';perfume: scan found no scents.'
    respond "  'sniff my #{VIAL}' returned: #{sniff_debug}"
    respond "  the name must work with 'sniff my <name>' by hand -- e.g. ';perfume set vial vial'."
  else
    save_scents(scents)
    scan_window_close("Done -- #{scents.size} scents recorded.\nClose this window.")
    respond ";perfume: recorded #{scents.size} scents -> #{SCENT_FILE}"
    respond "  use ';perfume scents' to review the list anytime."
  end
  respond ''
  exit
end

# Everything past here applies the perfume, so it must be configured:
# always a vial/item name, plus a bag when in bag mode.
if VIAL.empty? || (MODE == 'bag' && BAG.empty?)
  prompt_setup
  exit
end

if sub == 'once'
  refresh_perfume
  exit
end

# Safety net: whatever happens (normal stop, ;perfume stop, error), make sure
# we never leave a script paused that we paused.
before_dying do
  resume_scripts($perfume_paused)
  $perfume_paused = []
  DownstreamHook.remove('perfume_fade_watch') rescue nil
end

# Backup trigger: re-apply the instant the scent wears off. The first pattern
# is the exact, confirmed perfume fade message; the rest are conservative
# fallbacks in case a particular item ever uses custom wording.
fade_patterns = [
  /^The subtle scent which had been clinging to you dissipates\./i,
  /^The (?:scent|fragrance|aroma|perfume|cologne|sillage) .*(?:fade|wane|dissipate|dies|worn off|wear off)/i,
  /^You no longer (?:smell|reek|exude|carry the scent)/i,
  /^Your (?:scent|fragrance|perfume|cologne|sillage) (?:has |finally )?(?:faded|dissipated|worn off|waned)/i,
]
DownstreamHook.add('perfume_fade_watch', proc { |line|
  begin
    if fade_patterns.any? { |pat| line =~ pat }
      Thread.new { refresh_perfume rescue nil }
    end
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end
  line
})

respond ''
respond ";perfume: monitoring -- re-applying every #{REAPPLY_HOURS}h (scent lasts 4h). Timer is saved across logins."
respond ''

# `;perfume now` forces an immediate application and resets the timer.
refresh_perfume if sub == 'now'

# Timer loop. Uses the saved timestamp so the schedule survives logout: it
# computes how long is really left, waits that out (or applies right away if
# the interval already elapsed while logged off). The wear-off hook may reset
# the timestamp mid-wait; on wake we just recompute, so there's no double POUR.
loop do
  last      = UserVars.perfume_last_applied.to_i
  remaining = REAPPLY_SECS - (Time.now.to_i - last)
  if remaining > 0
    sleep remaining
  else
    sleep 60 unless refresh_perfume # back off on failure to avoid a tight retry loop
  end
end
